(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["command-of-evidence_10"] = [{"id":"0113152f","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"American fashion designer Patrick Kelly was known for his love of colorful buttons. Many of his signature dresses feature bold assortments of buttons throughout the garment. In a paper, a fashion design student claims that Kelly’s use of buttons as decoration was inspired by his childhood observations of the styles and actions of the women in his family. Which quotation from a work by a historian would be the most effective evidence for","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"American fashion designer Patrick Kelly was known for his love of colorful buttons. Many of his signature dresses feature bold assortments of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"buttons throughout the garment. In a paper, a fashion design student claims that Kelly’s use of buttons as decoration was inspired by his","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"childhood observations of the styles and actions of the women in his family.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation would be the most effective evidence for the student to include in support of this claim?","choices":["“Although some of the assortments of buttons appear to be mismatched pieces scattered randomly throughout Kelly’s dresses, his most famous designs feature carefully crafted patterns of matching buttons.”","“Many of Kelly’s contemporaries were inspired by his designs to incorporate buttons, as well as zippers and snaps, as decorative items in their work.”","“Kelly’s grandmother, who would repair clothing when he was a child, frequently added mismatched buttons to the clothes to draw attention away from any flaws in the garments.”","“Kelly was destined to be a designer from a young age: he learned how to sew clothing from his aunt Bertha, and his love of drawing was developed by his mother.”"]},{"id":"e441da80","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Investigative Articles Published in the Albuquerque Journal from 2010 to 2019 1,750 1,500 Number of articles 1,250 1,000 750 500 250 0 10 011 012 013 014 015 016 017 018 019 20 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 Total Investigative journalists research and report about fraud, corruption, public hazards, and more. The graph shows the number of investigative articles published in the Albuquerque Journal newspaper from 2010 to 2019. According to an analyst, although the number of investigative articles published in this newspaper has varied significantly over the period shown, the number overall has fallen since 2010.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Investigative Articles Published in the Albuquerque Journal, 2010–2019 — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Investigative journalists research and report about fraud, corruption, public hazards, and more. The graph shows the number of investigative articles published in the Albuquerque Journal newspaper from 2010 to 2019. According to an analyst, although the number of investigative articles published in this newspaper has varied significantly over the period shown, the number overall has fallen since 2010."}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to justify the underlined claim?","choices":["The newspaper published approximately 1,000 investigative articles in 2010 and approximately 500 in 2019.","The smallest annual number of investigative articles published in the newspaper during the period shown is approximately 1,600 in 2013.","The greatest annual number of investigative articles published in the newspaper during the period shown is approximately 1,000 in 2017.","The newspaper published approximately 1,000 investigative articles in 2010 and approximately 1,600 in 2013."],"underline":"the number overall has fallen since 2010.","underline_segments":["the number overall has fallen since 2010."]},{"id":"8a584241","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Seed Germination with and without H₂S Treatment 100 90 Seeds germinated (%) 80 70 60 50 40 30 20 10 0 24 48 72 168 Time (hours) 500 micromoles per liter 10 micromoles per liter untreated In high concentrations, hydrogen sulfide (H₂S) is typically toxic to many plants. Frederick D. Dooley and colleagues wanted to understand what effects low doses of H₂S might have on plant growth. They treated bean, corn, wheat, and pea seeds with various concentrations (measured in micromoles per liter) of H₂S and tracked the germination of those seeds along with the germination of untreated seeds. Treatment with particular concentrations of H₂S was associated with accelerated germination: for example, ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Seed Germination with and without H₂S Treatment — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"In high concentrations, hydrogen sulfide (H₂S) is typically toxic to many plants. Frederick D. Dooley and colleagues wanted to understand what effects low doses of H₂S might have on plant growth. They treated bean, corn, wheat, and pea seeds with various concentrations (measured in micromoles per liter) of H₂S and tracked the germination of those seeds along with the germination of untreated seeds. Treatment with particular concentrations of H₂S was associated with accelerated germination: for example, ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the statement?","choices":["at 24 hours, less than 10% of seeds treated with H₂S at a concentration of 10 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas more than 90% of those seeds had germinated at 168 hours.","at 48 hours, more than 70% of seeds treated with H₂S at a concentration of 10 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas only approximately 50% of untreated seeds had germinated.","at 168 hours, more than 90% of seeds treated with H₂S at concentrations of 10 or 500 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas less than 70% of untreated seeds had germinated.",""],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"e946a32e","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Boldly mixing elements of poetry, fiction, drama, philosophy, and manifesto, Puerto Rican writer Giannina Braschi creates cross-genre literature that explores themes such as immigration and independence. Her works have inspired responses from individuals across different fields and in a wide range of formats, from musical compositions and a comic book to architecture and furniture design. In an essay, a student asserts that the production of these diverse creations by others is reflective of Braschi’s own approach to crafting literature. Which quotation from a scholarly review of Braschi’s work best supports","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Boldly mixing elements of poetry, fiction, drama, philosophy, and manifesto, Puerto Rican writer Giannina Braschi creates cross-genre literature","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that explores themes such as immigration and independence. Her works have inspired responses from individuals across different fields and in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"a wide range of formats, from musical compositions and a comic book to architecture and furniture design. In an essay, a student asserts that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the production of these diverse creations by others is reflective of Braschi’s own approach to crafting literature.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from a literary critic would best support the student’s claim?","choices":["“Braschi is the focus of a 2020 collection of essays in which fifteen scholars from seven different countries delved into the linguistic and structural patterns of her writings.”","“Braschi’s eagerness to push boundaries and blend genres within literature invites us to consider how other art forms might also engage with literature.”","“Before settling in New York City, where she would go on to become a college professor, Braschi studied both literature and philosophy in several cities around the world.”","“In addition to her creative literary works, Braschi has produced academic pieces analyzing writings by Miguel de Cervantes, Federico García Lorca, and other authors.”"]},{"id":"3d91c973","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Mosasaurs were large marine reptiles that lived in the Late Cretaceous period, approximately 100 million to 66 million years ago. Celina Suarez, Alberto Pérez-Huerta, and T. Lynn Harrell Jr. examined oxygen-18 isotopes in mosasaur tooth enamel","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Mosasaurs were large marine reptiles that lived in the Late Cretaceous period, approximately 100 million to 66 million years ago. Celina Suarez,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Alberto Pérez-Huerta, and T. Lynn Harrell Jr. examined oxygen-18 isotopes in mosasaur tooth enamel in order to calculate likely mosasaur body","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"temperatures and determined that mosasaurs were endothermic—that is, they used internal metabolic processes to maintain a stable body","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"temperature in a variety of ambient temperatures. Suarez, Pérez-Huerta, and Harrell claim that endothermy would have enabled mosasaurs to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"include relatively cold polar waters in their range.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Suarez, Pérez-Huerta, and Harrell’s claim?","choices":["Mosasaurs likely body temperatures are easier to determine from tooth enamel oxygen-18 isotope data than the body temperatures of nonendothermic Late Cretaceous marine reptiles are.","Fossils of both mosasaurs and nonendothermic marine reptiles have been found in roughly equal numbers in regions known to be near the poles during the Late Cretaceous, though in lower concentrations than elsewhere.","Several mosasaur fossils have been found in regions known to be near the poles during the Late Cretaceous, while relatively few fossils of nonendothermic marine reptiles have been found in those locations.","During the Late Cretaceous, seawater temperatures were likely higher throughout mosasaurs range, including near the poles, than seawater temperatures at those same latitudes are today."]},{"id":"d76ea360","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean Sea. Indigenous people there started raising guinea pigs about 1,700 years ago. Guinea pigs had originally been domesticated much earlier in both Colombia and Peru. So were guinea pigs brought to Puerto Rico from Colombia or from Peru? Ancient Caribbean trade routes connected Puerto Rico with Colombia but not with Peru. Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean Sea. Indigenous people there started raising guinea pigs about 1,700 years ago. Guinea pigs had","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"originally been domesticated much earlier in both Colombia and Peru. So were guinea pigs brought to Puerto Rico from Colombia or from Peru?","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Ancient Caribbean trade routes connected Puerto Rico with Colombia but not with Peru. Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the underlined claim?","choices":["Ancient guinea pigs in Puerto Rico were genetically less similar to ancient guinea pigs in Colombia than to ancient guinea pigs in Peru.","Guinea pigs are common in ancient Puerto Rican art, especially in pottery.","Modern breeds of guinea pigs don’t look like images of guinea pigs in ancient art from Puerto Rico, Colombia, and Peru.","The guinea pig population of ancient Colombia was much larger than the guinea pig population of ancient Peru."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came","from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs."]},{"id":"b30a2613","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Spider Population Count 90 80 70 60 Spider count 50 40 30 20 10 0 1 10 20 30 Day of experiment no lizards with lizards To investigate the effect of lizard predation on spider populations, a student in a biology class placed spiders in two enclosures, one with lizards and one without, and tracked the number of spiders in the enclosures for 30 days. The student concluded that the reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was entirely attributable to the presence of the lizards.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Spider Population Count — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"To investigate the effect of lizard predation on spider populations, a student in a biology class placed spiders in two enclosures, one with lizards and one without, and tracked the number of spiders in the enclosures for 30 days. The student concluded that the reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was entirely attributable to the presence of the lizards."}],"question":"Which choice best describes data from the graph that weaken the student’s conclusion?","choices":["The spider population count was the same in both enclosures on day 1.","The spider population count also substantially declined by day 30 in the enclosure without lizards.","The largest decline in spider population count in the enclosure with lizards occurred from day 1 to day 10.","The spider population count on day 30 was lower in the enclosure with lizards than in the enclosure without lizards."]},{"id":"0021d326","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Olms are salamanders that live in underwater caves. Scientists once thought that olms stay in their caves all their lives. However, Raoul Manenti and team claim that olms regularly come to the surface to perform important activities such as finding food.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Olms are salamanders that live in underwater caves. Scientists once thought that olms stay in their caves all their lives. However, Raoul Manenti","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and team claim that olms regularly come to the surface to perform important activities such as finding food.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most strongly support the underlined claim?","choices":["Researchers determine that olms don’t breed often.","Researchers confirm that olms live in only a few cave systems.","Researchers discover that earthworms from surface soils are a major part of olms’ diet.","Researchers learn that olms’ brains differ from other salamanders’ brains."],"underline":"olms regularly come to the surface to perform important activities such as finding food.","underline_segments":["olms regularly come to the surface to perform important activities such as finding food."]},{"id":"30c3aa98","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Copper Production for Three States, 1889-1909 400 Yearly copper production (in millions of pounds) 300 200 100 0 1889 1902 1909 Year Montana Arizona Michigan Copper had been mined in the US for thousands of years, but large-scale commercial mining of copper took off starting in the late 1800s. This was due to several factors. Technological advancements in the mining industry led to improvements in the production of copper. This helped the country keep up with the growing number of people wanting to buy copper starting in the 1890s. At the same time, the growth of the railroad system made the transportation of copper in large batches much easier. Several states saw rapid growth in the production of this resource, for example: ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Copper Production for Three States, 1889–1909 — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Copper had been mined in the US for thousands of years, but large-scale commercial mining of copper took off starting in the late 1800s. This was due to several factors. Technological advancements in the mining industry led to improvements in the production of copper. This helped the country keep up with the growing number of people wanting to buy copper starting in the 1890s. At the same time, the growth of the railroad system made the transportation of copper in large batches much easier. Several states saw rapid growth in the production of this resource, for example: ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses the data in the graph to complete the example?","choices":["The rise in copper production in Michigan slowed from 1902 to 1909.","Montana and Arizona produced more copper than Michigan did in 1909.","Fewer than 100 million pounds of copper were produced in Arizona in 1889.","Copper production rose significantly from 1889 to 1909 for Arizona, Michigan, and Montana."]},{"id":"d52fca9f","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Many music streaming services also function as social media platforms: by giving users the option to follow friends and share curated playlists or information about their listening history, these platforms allow people to convey their music preferences and listening activities directly to their social networks. In a 2023 study, researcher Michael James Walsh interviewed frequent users of a popular music streaming platform to investigate how its social media dimensions shape their listening habits. Walsh found that these dimensions tended to make study participants feel more mindful of how their listening activities may be perceived, which in turn influenced how they managed those activities.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Many music streaming services also function as social media platforms: by giving users the option to follow friends and share curated playlists","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"or information about their listening history, these platforms allow people to convey their music preferences and listening activities directly to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"their social networks. In a 2023 study, researcher Michael James Walsh interviewed frequent users of a popular music streaming platform to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"investigate how its social media dimensions shape their listening habits. Walsh found that these dimensions tended to make study participants","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"feel more mindful of how their listening activities may be perceived, which in turn influenced how they managed those activities.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from a music streaming platform user would best illustrate Walsh’s finding?","choices":["“When I create playlists or choose songs to listen to, I often pick songs that I think the friends who are following me might be interested in listening to, rather than what I might actually prefer listening to in that moment.”","“Because the predictions the platform makes about what new songs I might like depend on my past listening habits, at times its recommendations can feel overly repetitive and unvarying.”","“The social aspects of music streaming make it really easy to create a sense of a shared listening experience with my friends, even if we aren’t in the same room.”","“Listening to music through a streaming platform feels a lot more passive, since I don’t need to make any deliberate choices about what music I’m going to consume, like I do when buying digital downloads or records and CDs.”"]},{"id":"e37f79a7","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Housing Starts in the US, January –April 2022 (in thousands) Month Housing starts January 1,669 February 1,771 March 1,713 April 1,803 When construction of a single-family house begins, it is called a housing start. In the first four months of 2022, the highest number of housing starts in the United States was in ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"table","title":"Housing Starts in the US, January–April 2022 (in thousands)","headers":["Month","Housing starts"],"rows":[["January","1,669"],["February","1,771"],["March","1,713"],["April","1,803"]]},{"type":"text","text":"When construction of a single-family house begins, it is called a housing start. In the first four months of 2022, the highest number of housing starts in the United States was in ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?","choices":["April.","March.","January.","February."]},{"id":"c088a9a9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Over the course of the 1900s, more and more Native Hawaiians spoke English instead of the Hawaiian language. To preserve their language, Native Hawaiian teachers founded the Aha P ‘ ūnana Leo preschool in 1984. They spoke Hawaiian while teaching, and their Native Hawaiian students were soon able to understand and speak it themselves. The school was a huge success. Eventually it opened locations around Hawai i ‘ and started teaching Hawaiian to elementary and high school students too. Thanks to Aha P ‘ ūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak the language has increased.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Over the course of the 1900s, more and more Native Hawaiians spoke English instead of the Hawaiian language. To preserve their language,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Native Hawaiian teachers founded the ‘Aha Pūnana Leo preschool in 1984. They spoke Hawaiian while teaching, and their Native Hawaiian","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"students were soon able to understand and speak it themselves. The school was a huge success. Eventually it opened locations around Hawai‘i","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and started teaching Hawaiian to elementary and high school students too. Thanks to ‘Aha Pūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the language has increased.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement, if true, would most directly support the underlined claim?","choices":["Fewer than fifty children could speak Hawaiian when Aha P ūnana Leo was founded, but now more than 2,000 students at ‘Aha Pūnana Leo speak it.","Roughly 680,000 Native Hawaiian people lived in the United States in 2020, and a little less than half of them lived in Hawai i. ‘","Hawaiian is very similar to other languages that are spoken on the Polynesian Islands of the Pacific Ocean, including Tahitian, Samoan, and M āori. ‘","Besides Native Hawaiians, tens of thousands of people from other Pacific Islander communities live in Hawai i today, including over 37,000 Samoans."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Thanks to ‘Aha Pūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak","the language has increased."]},{"id":"5b74feb9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Political scientists who favor the traditional view of voter behavior claim that voting in an election does not change a voter’s attitude toward the candidates in that election. Focusing on each US presidential election from 1976 to 1996, Ebonya Washington and Sendhil Mullainathan tested this claim by distinguishing between subjects who had just become old enough to vote (around half of whom actually voted) and otherwise similar subjects who were slightly too young to vote (and thus none of whom voted). Washington and Mullainathan compared the attitudes of the groups of subjects toward the winning candidate two years after each election.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Political scientists who favor the traditional view of voter behavior claim that voting in an election does not change a voter’s attitude toward the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"candidates in that election. Focusing on each US presidential election from 1976 to 1996, Ebonya Washington and Sendhil Mullainathan tested","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"this claim by distinguishing between subjects who had just become old enough to vote (around half of whom actually voted) and otherwise","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"similar subjects who were slightly too young to vote (and thus none of whom voted). Washington and Mullainathan compared the attitudes of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the groups of subjects toward the winning candidate two years after each election.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding from Washington and Mullainathan’s study, if true, would most directly weaken the claim made by people who favor the traditional view of voter behavior?","choices":["Subjects’ attitudes toward the winning candidate two years after a given election were strongly predicted by subjects’ general political orientation, regardless of whether subjects were old enough to vote at the time of the election.","Subjects who were not old enough to vote in a given election held significantly more positive attitudes towards the winning candidate two years later than they held at the time of the election.","Subjects who voted in a given election held significantly more polarized attitudes toward the winning candidate two years later than did subjects who were not old enough to vote in that election.","Two years after a given election, subjects who voted and subjects who were not old enough to vote were significantly more likely to express negative attitudes than positive attitudes toward the winning candidate in that election."]},{"id":"e2829dd7","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Number of Infrared Beam Breaks by Mice Treated with CNO or Saline, by Sex 1,500 Number of beam breaks 1,000 500 0 -4 10 24 38 52 66 80 94 108 122 136 150 Minutes from treatment females with saline males with saline males with CNO females with CNO To investigate the influence of certain estrogen-responsive neurons on energy expenditure, biologist Stephanie Correa et al. treated female and male mice with either saline solution or clozapine-N4-oxide (CNO), which activates the neurons. Monitoring the activity levels of the mice by measuring how frequently the animals broke infrared beams crossing their enclosures, Correa et al. found that the mice in their study showed sex-specific differences in response to neuron activation: ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Number of Infrared Beam Breaks by Mice Treated with CNO or Saline, by Sex — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"To investigate the influence of certain estrogen-responsive neurons on energy expenditure, biologist Stephanie Correa et al. treated female and male mice with either saline solution or clozapine-N4-oxide (CNO), which activates the neurons. Monitoring the activity levels of the mice by measuring how frequently the animals broke infrared beams crossing their enclosures, Correa et al. found that the mice in their study showed sex-specific differences in response to neuron activation: ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?","choices":["the four groups of mice differed greatly in their activity levels before treatment but showed identical activity levels at the end of the monitoring period.","saline-treated females showed substantially more activity at certain points in the monitoring period than saline-treated males did.","CNO-treated females showed more activity relative to saline-treated females than CNO-treated males showed relative to saline-treated males.","CNO-treated males showed a substantial decline in activity during the monitoring period, followed by a steep increase in activity at the end."]}];
